# One CI gate, one file. Issue #991 moved the gate list out of
# `.github/workflows/release.yml`, the repository's third most conflicted path,
# because its step list was append-only. A gate lives here instead, so two
# branches adding gates create two files, never one shared region.
# `rust-script scripts/run-ci-gates.rs --stage <stage>` runs them.
#
# The system diagrams under docs/diagrams/ (issue #538, R382) are generated
# from live data: the handler precedence and promotion seeds, the clap CLI
# definition and the server route manifest. A seed, CLI or route edit that
# is committed without regenerating them leaves the published architecture
# view describing a system that no longer exists, so this gate re-renders
# them and fails on any byte of drift. The Rust twin is pinned to the same
# committed parts by rust/tests/unit/system_diagrams.rs.
ci_gate check-system-diagrams
  stage web
  description "The generated system diagrams in docs/diagrams/ (overview, solver handlers, CLI subcommands, HTTP routes) are byte-current against the live seed, CLI definition and route manifest."
  run "node scripts/generate-system-diagrams.mjs --check"
  justification "Issue #538 (R382) asked for generated, split mermaid diagrams of every entry point; a hand-maintained or stale diagram silently misdescribes routing, so the committed parts must equal what the generator renders from the live sources."
